  "addition": " Fill the fields separately. For route, choose what the worker should do first. For current_obligations, report the outcomes still owed in the chosen package. For each ID, check its own completion field and the receipt that establishes the debt: include UNSATISFIED or STALE commitments even if BLOCKED; leave SATISFIED and UNKNOWN candidates out. Ask what would still be owed immediately after a lookup. Put the lookup in route only when it serves that outcome; list it also as a commitment only if producing the evidence is itself explicitly owed. A ready route, a missing receipt, and an unchosen alternative do not by themselves establish another debt. Keep a shared failure at its evidenced scope; preserve the chosen package's recorded gaps. Copy probe_completion and probe_readiness literally from the node named by probed_obligation, even if the route uses another node.",
  "scope": "Prompt-only v240.4. BASE=v240.3 submission-r2 TEXT. TEXT=replace its field guidance, preserving the terminal tool instruction. Unchanged v240 compiler, no projection. 15 main + 4 prior challenge + 3 additional historical boundaries not used in v240.3 prompt comparisons + 1 masked control. Two fresh calls per site per arm, counterbalanced; no resampling or Worker runs.",
  "scoring": "Primary raw exact on main, secondary confirm over-inclusion and consensus retention. Adopt only if main raw exact improves, consensus raw retention does not fall, and both probes valid without change. Preserve original gate. Separate prior challenge and additional three; report targeted dependency raw and first-step paired counts, structural validity, state readout and cost. Development estimates only.",
  "terminal_instruction": " Submit the arguments through exactly one activate_organization tool call. A JSON object written in the assistant message does not execute the plan."
}
